# Which matrix tags survive entry-by-entry operations (see the spec, "Arrays:
# entry by entry"): Symmetric when both operands are, Diagonal for `*` when
# either operand is and for `/` when the numerator is; never PositiveDefinite
# or Orthogonal. A function of a matrix keeps Symmetric only.
S: Symmetric Matrix[3, 3]
D: Diagonal Matrix[3, 3]
P: PositiveDefinite Matrix[3, 3]
Q: Orthogonal Matrix[3, 3]
GM: Matrix[3, 3]
ss = S * S
sd = S * D
dg = GM * D
dgg = D * GM
pp = P * P
qq = Q * Q
sp = S * P
dq = D / GM
gd = GM / D
ssq = S / S
sqrtS = sqrt(S)
sqrtD = sqrt(D)
sqrtP = sqrt(P)
sq = sqrt(Q)
hy = hypot(S, S)
hg = hypot(S, GM)
mx = max(S, 1)
